WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.056 --> 00:00:10.506
That year the children were especially proud of their contributions to Thanksgiving dinner.

2
00:00:10.507 --> 00:00:17.147
"My herbs made the stuffing really delicious," Nan said with her mouth full.

3
00:00:17.148 --> 00:00:25.060
Jack scooped another potato onto his plate and said, "These are the best potatoes I've ever eaten!"

4
00:00:25.061 --> 00:00:29.355
"Has everyone had some of my beans?" Nat asked.

5
00:00:29.356 --> 00:00:38.232
"Of course!" Tommy said. "You grew so many that Asia said we must all eat three helpings!"

6
00:00:38.233 --> 00:00:44.497
"The pies came from my giant pumpkin," Rob said, "and wait till you see—"

7
00:00:44.498 --> 00:00:52.551
"Hush!" Daisy said, giving her cousin a gentle swat. "It's a surprise!"

8
00:00:52.552 --> 00:00:56.746
But the professor had overheard them and was curious.

9
00:00:56.747 --> 00:01:02.530
"Daisy, I know you helped bake many pies, but Rob's pumpkin was enormous.

10
00:01:02.531 --> 00:01:05.867
What did you do with the rest of it?"

11
00:01:05.868 --> 00:01:10.846
"Well . . . uh . . . " Daisy hesitated.

12
00:01:10.847 --> 00:01:17.158
Dan rescued Daisy by handing a bowl of nuts to Mr. Bauer. "Sir, try these!"

13
00:01:17.159 --> 00:01:28.205
The professor looked down the table, murmuring to Jo, "Everyone seems to be in on this secret except me, but I can wait."

14
00:01:28.206 --> 00:01:33.221
After dinner they all went for a long walk.

15
00:01:33.222 --> 00:01:37.319
Then they waited impatiently for the rest of the family to arrive:

16
00:01:37.320 --> 00:01:45.961
Mr. and Mrs. March, Aunt Meg and baby Josy, Uncle Laurie and Aunt Amy with Bess and a special guest.

17
00:01:45.962 --> 00:01:55.216
"Mr. Hyde!" Dan exclaimed, immediately recognizing the naturalist. "What are you doing here?"

18
00:01:55.217 --> 00:02:01.178
"I thought he'd like to see how well you're doing," Laurie said. "We're so proud of you."

19
00:02:01.179 --> 00:02:08.119
"What a fine, polite young man you've turned into," Mr. Hyde said to Dan.

20
00:02:08.120 --> 00:02:15.806
Dan and Mr. Hyde went to a parlor to talk until it was time for the evening's entertainment.

21
00:02:15.807 --> 00:02:24.852
Then everyone went into the schoolroom, where Jack amazed the audience by solving math problems in his head.

22
00:02:24.853 --> 00:02:33.205
Tommy won the spelling bee, and Dan performed gymnastics.

23
00:02:33.206 --> 00:02:38.095
"Dan's a strong lad," Mr. Hyde said to the professor.

24
00:02:38.096 --> 00:02:43.512
"When I go to South America in a few years, I'd like to take him along."

25
00:02:43.513 --> 00:02:50.802
Overhearing that remark, Dan smiled, grateful to both Mr. Hyde and the Bauers.

26
00:02:50.803 --> 00:02:56.136
"Where did the other children go?" the professor asked.

27
00:02:56.137 --> 00:03:01.963
"Back here!" said a muffled voice behind a curtain made of blankets.

28
00:03:01.964 --> 00:03:10.070
"Shh!" said more voices amid lots of giggles.

29
00:03:10.071 --> 00:03:14.398
The curtain rose to reveal Bess as Cinderella.

30
00:03:14.399 --> 00:03:24.687
Dressed in a ragged pinafore, she sat before a cardboard fireplace, not moving until Daisy whispered loudly, "Now!"

31
00:03:24.688 --> 00:03:30.759
"Oh, I wish I could go to the ball!" Cinderella said.

32
00:03:30.760 --> 00:03:38.617
Laurie clapped enthusiastically for his daughter, and Amy whispered, "My little darling!"

33
00:03:38.618 --> 00:03:45.683
"You must not speak to me!" scolded Cinderella, looking at her parents.

34
00:03:45.684 --> 00:03:51.934
The back of the fireplace opened like a door, and Nan appeared as the fairy godmother.

35
00:03:51.935 --> 00:03:58.272
Dressed in a red cloak and pointed hat, she struggled to get through the opening.

36
00:03:58.273 --> 00:04:06.007
"You shall go to the ball!" the fairy godmother said, tapping Cinderella with her wand.

37
00:04:06.008 --> 00:04:13.001
"Now you must show my pretty dress," Cinderella said, tugging on her pinafore.

38
00:04:13.002 --> 00:04:21.395
"No, no," Nan said in her own voice. "First you say, 'How can I go in these rags?'"

39
00:04:21.396 --> 00:04:27.264
"Oh, that's right!" Cinderella said, and repeated Nan's words.

40
00:04:27.265 --> 00:04:36.283
With that, the fairy godmother unfastened Cinderella's pinafore to reveal a beautiful pink dress.

41
00:04:36.284 --> 00:04:42.756
She placed a crown on Cinderella's head and gave her silver paper slippers.

42
00:04:42.757 --> 00:04:49.277
"But you have no coach!" the fairy godmother declared, waving her wand.

43
00:04:49.278 --> 00:04:58.411
Cinderella was too busy admiring her slippers to say her next line, so Silas just leaped into action from backstage.

44
00:04:58.412 --> 00:05:03.418
"Ready, Daisy?" he whispered. "Push!"

45
00:05:03.419 --> 00:05:12.475
Suddenly four rats appeared, pulling a magnificent coach made from Rob's pumpkin and Teddy's wagon.

46
00:05:12.476 --> 00:05:18.923
As the coachman, Teddy helped Cinderella into the coach and squeezed in beside her.

47
00:05:18.924 --> 00:05:24.953
Cinderella waved to the audience, and that was the end of the first scene.

48
00:05:24.954 --> 00:05:31.790
In the ball scene, Rob played the prince while Nan and Daisy were the stepsisters.

49
00:05:31.791 --> 00:05:41.658
The prince and Cinderella danced and danced until finally Nan had to whisper, "Cinderella, drop your shoe!"

50
00:05:41.659 --> 00:05:51.458
"Oops, I forgot!" gasped Cinderella, taking off a slipper and planting it in the middle of the stage before running away.

51
00:05:51.459 --> 00:06:01.153
In the last scene, the prince and the coachman arrived with the slipper, which didn't fit the stepsisters—only Cinderella.

52
00:06:01.154 --> 00:06:07.492
"I'm the princess!" Cinderella announced, running over to her parents.

53
00:06:07.493 --> 00:06:10.621
"Didn't I do a good job?"

54
00:06:10.622 --> 00:06:15.449
"It was a beautiful play!" Laurie said.

55
00:06:15.450 --> 00:06:21.541
"And now I know what happened to the pumpkin," the professor said with a smile.

56
00:06:21.542 --> 00:06:27.888
Following the play, Nat played a sweet song on his violin.

57
00:06:27.889 --> 00:06:35.521
When he finished, he bowed to Jo, saying, "Mr. Laurence wrote that piece for you."

58
00:06:35.522 --> 00:06:39.235
"Oh, thank you, Laurie," Jo said.

59
00:06:39.236 --> 00:06:42.870
"You're the one who deserves thanks," Laurie said.

60
00:06:42.871 --> 00:06:45.827
"Look at what you've done for these children.

61
00:06:45.828 --> 00:06:51.850
Nat, Dan, and Nan—and the others—are all so much better and so full of promise.

62
00:06:51.851 --> 00:06:56.786
And after John died, you comforted the twins as if they were your own children.

63
00:06:56.787 --> 00:07:01.291
When Bess is old enough, I want her to go to Plumfield."

64
00:07:01.292 --> 00:07:04.319
Jo couldn't resist teasing him.

65
00:07:04.320 --> 00:07:10.084
"I thought you were unsure about boys and girls at school together."

66
00:07:10.085 --> 00:07:16.197
"Not anymore, and now you must excuse me for a moment," Laurie said, slipping away.

67
00:07:16.198 --> 00:07:23.692
He soon returned with all the children, who formed a circle around Jo and the professor.

68
00:07:23.693 --> 00:07:31.163
Together they sang a Thanksgiving song, and at the end, the circle tightened into a hug.

69
00:07:31.164 --> 00:07:43.497
There was one plant that had taken root in all of Plumfield's gardens this year, and that was love.

